      "comment": "ARAMINTA (7) earns top billing after producing a strong Toowoomba win in BM60 grade, overcoming a slow beginning and a held-up moment before getting home by a nose from Turf Gazette. Her previous Sunshine Coast third in BM58 grade was also sound, and the return on a quick back-up at an easier meeting gives her a solid winning case. CAPITAL ASSET (2) is the established danger after leading throughout at Warwick as favourite and beating The Catch by a nose, with his earlier BM85 effort at Toowoomba adding depth to the profile despite a mixed 1600m record. VILLADEN (3) brings consistent country form, having won a Quality at Taroom before a narrow Tara second, though this is a harder meeting and he has to carry 61kg. JUSTICE SERVED (6) has been plain at Gold Coast and Sunshine Coast, but the quick back-up, easier company and solid good-track record give him some chance to improve into the placings.",
